firmware/ includes firmware/lib/skeumo_link, which comes from the same
author's Skeumo project and is licensed here under GPL-3.0-or-later as well.

  - Code (GPL-3.0-or-later): firmware you distribute, including firmware
    flashed onto a device you sell or give away, must come with its complete
    corresponding source under the GPL.
  - Hardware designs (CERN-OHL-S-2.0): the OpenSCAD source and STL files.
    If you make and distribute products from them (printed parts, kits,
    finished devices), keep the notices, make your modified design source
    available, and point to it from the product or its documentation.
  - Documentation and media (CC-BY-SA-4.0): credit "Firewatch by
    micahflock" with a link to https://github.com/micahflock/Firewatch and
    the license, say whether you changed anything, and share adaptations
    under CC-BY-SA-4.0.

Third-party libraries the firmware downloads at build time (NeoPixelBus,
HomeSpan, NimBLE-Arduino, IRremoteESP8266, Unity) are not part of this
repository and keep their own licenses, all compatible with GPL-3.0.
